	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Setup

Grant Alfred Accessibility permission in System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Accessibility. Apple provides no API for the Passwords app, so this workflow controls it through the Accessibility API.

Requires macOS Sequoia or later.

## Usage

Search your Apple Passwords entries and copy a field to the clipboard via the `pass` keyword.

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy the password.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy the username.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy the verification code.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌃&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Copy the website.

The clipboard is cleared after the delay set in the Workflow’s Configuration, but only if it still holds the copied value.

Alternatively, save the Passwords app’s accessibility tree to your Desktop via the `pwdump` keyword. Use it if a field cannot be found. The dump is redacted — your entries are replaced with character counts — so it is safe to attach to a bug report.
</string>
